CA6B = 'https://dot.ca.gov/-/media/dot-media/programs/safety-programs/documents/ca-mutcd/2026/2026-camutcd-2026-6b-a11y.pdf'
st('tc-ca-signspacing-1', 'CA', 'California advance warning sign spacing by speed (CA MUTCD Table 6B-1)', T_SIGN,
   "California's Table 6B-1 in the CA MUTCD 2026 sets advance warning sign spacing by speed on urban streets, which the national table does not. Distances A, B and C are the same within each row. Urban, 25 mph or less: 100 ft. 30 mph: 150 ft. 35 mph: 200 ft. 40 mph: 250 ft. 45 mph: 300 ft. Urban, 50 mph or more: 350 ft. Rural: 500 ft. Expressway or freeway: A 1,000 ft, B 1,500 ft, C 2,640 ft. A is from the taper or point of restriction to the first sign, B from the first to the second sign, C from the second to the third. Use the posted speed limit, the off-peak 85th-percentile speed before work starts, or the expected operating speed. So three signs on a 35 mph city street sit 200 ft apart, 600 ft in all. These are recommended minimums; the encroachment permit or the approved traffic control plan can ask for more, and on State highways the Caltrans Standard Plans govern.",
   'CA MUTCD 2026 (Caltrans, eff. Jan. 18, 2026), Table 6B-1 and footnotes; Section 6B.04', CA6B, 'CA MUTCD 2026', '2026-01-18')
